    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "568b3d30_a2187d72",
        "filename": "zephyr/drivers/fingerprint/fingerprint_egis_ec6601_pal.c",
        "patchSetId": 7
      },
      "lineNbr": 29,
      "author": {
        "id": 4412439
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-12-08T09:26:25Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "It\u0027s a workaround for leave_cs_asserted where write_pending occupies a maximum of 1 bytes.",
      "parentUuid": "04c4c259_69c3b605",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 29,
        "startChar": 15,
        "endLine": 29,
        "endChar": 31
      },
      "revId": "d521ab3aa75239138dbfac7e5df88e4bb47df40b",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "51f2a9b6_bd108bb3",
        "filename": "zephyr/drivers/fingerprint/fingerprint_egis_ec6601_pal.c",
        "patchSetId": 7
      },
      "lineNbr": 63,
      "author": {
        "id": 1541085
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-11-20T22:36:52Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "egis_malloc is called within the SPI function to create a temporary receive buffer (data_tmp). Dynamic allocation in low-level drivers, especially for I/O operations, can lead to latency issues, heap fragmentation, or failures. It\u0027s better to use pre-allocated buffers or stack arrays if the maximum size is known and reasonable.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 63,
        "startChar": 14,
        "endLine": 63,
        "endChar": 41
      },
      "revId": "d521ab3aa75239138dbfac7e5df88e4bb47df40b",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "31dcc202_c839f4c5",
        "filename": "zephyr/drivers/fingerprint/fingerprint_egis_ec6601_pal.c",
        "patchSetId": 7
      },
      "lineNbr": 63,
      "author": {
        "id": 4412439
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-12-08T09:26:25Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "The only happens at capturing image or do calibration, and it\u0027s not a fixed size. It\u0027s a workaround for now cause the cs can not be controlled.",
      "parentUuid": "51f2a9b6_bd108bb3",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 63,
        "startChar": 14,
        "endLine": 63,
        "endChar": 41
      },
      "revId": "d521ab3aa75239138dbfac7e5df88e4bb47df40b",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "8b917a3b_b0b1fb3c",
        "filename": "zephyr/drivers/fingerprint/fingerprint_egis_ec6601_pal.c",
